<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Gruma plans Europe tortilla plant.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Gruma plans Europe tortilla plant.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gruma SA, the Mexican holding company for tortilla giant Grupo Industrial Maseca, plans to open a tortilla plant in Europe in the near future, a company director said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the near future, we will have a tortilla plant in Europe,&quot; Eduardo Sastre, director of communications, told a news conference.</p>
<p>Sastre did not name the country that Gruma had earmarked for the tortilla plant or a specific timeframe. Tortillas are corn flour pancakes eaten more widely than bread in Mexico.</p>
<p>((--Tomas de la Rosa, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7912))</p>
